*  RED, CHECKED IN RED (law 0d).  ***AN ARBNO PRECEDED BY ANOTHER ELEMENT NEVER RETRIES,
*  AND THE STATEMENT RUNS AWAY.***  Reduced from corpus/programs/csnobol4-suite/breakx's
*  second statement (BREAK(' ') ARBNO(LEN(1) BREAK(' '))).  BREAKX itself is CURED (s192,
*  rty-fail-inline-retry) -- this is a DIFFERENT, still-open defect: ARBNO's own retry
*  wiring, when ARBNO is NOT the leftmost element of its (...)$ group.  The oracle prints
*  each extension t/th/thi/this/... up to the literal; SCRIP prints "this" forever.
*  ⛔ CAPTURE STDOUT WITH A HARD timeout WHEN RUNNING THIS -- SCRIP DOES NOT TERMINATE.
	&ANCHOR = 1
	subj = "this is a test ."
	subj (BREAK(' ') ARBNO(LEN(1))) $ OUTPUT '.'
END
